From 633e6f942fd32d834dd8f34d8acb824ce9312d4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:43:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] feat(gateway): refuse instance addresses outside the
 allowed networks

The stream proxy dialed any address written to status.endpoints, so an
endpoint pointing at 169.254.169.254 or an internal service turned the
gateway into a proxy for it.

The proxy now checks every resolved IP right before connecting
(net.Dialer.Control), which also holds when a host name later resolves
somewhere else. GATEWAY_INSTANCE_ALLOWED_CIDRS lists the networks
instances may live in; without it the gateway refuses loopback,
link-local (including the common metadata address), unspecified,
multicast and known metadata service addresses. Refused connections
return 502 INSTANCE_ADDRESS_NOT_ALLOWED and count as an instance
failure. make run-dev allows loopback instances.
